  "content": {
    "id": "p62-q8",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Apple weights from an orchard are normally distributed with standard deviation 15 g. 20% of apples weigh more than 185 g. Find the mean weight to 1 d.p.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$172.4\\text{ g}$",
      "worked": "$P(X\\le185)=1-0.20=0.80$.\n\nUsing inverse normal, $z=\\operatorname{invNorm}(0.80)\\approx0.8416$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}185&=\\mu+15\\operatorname{invNorm}(0.80)\\\\\\mu&=185-15\\operatorname{invNorm}(0.80)\\\\\\mu&\\approx172.4\\text{ g}\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
